commit 6abc7c431687a2037d007eaa6f195dc37d7a461a
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 18:17:32 2026 +1100

    db: Keep is_agent_down out of the agent utilities
    
    is_agent_down() lived in neutron.agent.common.utils, which pulls in
    pyroute2, oslo.privsep and neutron.privileged. The agent model and five
    other server modules use it, costing neutron-api and the RPC server 7
    to 9MB of anonymous memory each (117 to 110MB and 116 to 107MB).
    
    Move it to a new neutron.common.agent_status module and use that in
    tree. The old name remains as an alias, but mocking it no longer
    affects in-tree callers. Add a test that importing the agent model
    does not load pyroute2 or neutron.privileged.
    
    Prompt: Mikal asked for privsep memory fixes that can be landed one at a
    time and measured in devstack CI; neutron daemons are the largest.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    
    Change-Id: Ib49e83c5cd59aa84839fba9c06329735f922b042
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

